  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmployeeExperience>
    skos:definition "The sum total of an employee’s interactions with an organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmployeeWellbeing>
    skos:definition "Promoting the physical, mental and emotional health of employees."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MeaningfulWork>
    skos:definition "Providing employees with work that is challenging, engaging and aligned with their values."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WorkLifeBalance>
    skos:definition "Supporting employees in achieving a healthy balance between their work and personal lives."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WorkplaceFlexibility>
    skos:definition "Offering employees flexibility in their work arrangements, such as remote work options or flexible hours."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/HumanResourcesOperations>
    skos:definition "The fundamental, administrative functions of human resources that are essential for the daily management of a workforce"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BenefitsAdministration>
    skos:definition "Managing and administering employee benefits programs, such as health insurance, retirement plans, and paid time off."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CompensationManagement>
    skos:definition "Designing and implementing a company’s compensation system, including salaries, wages, bonuses, and other forms of remuneration."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmployeeDataManagement>
    skos:definition "Collecting, storing, and managing employee information securely and efficiently."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TimeAttendance>
    skos:definition "Tracking employee work hours, absences, and leave."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OrganizationalCulture>
    skos:definition "The shared values, beliefs and norms that shape the behavior of individuals within an organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CollaborationCommunication>
    skos:definition "Fostering teamwork and open communication within the organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DiversityInclusion>
    skos:definition "Creating a workplace that values and respects individuals from diverse backgrounds."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ValuesEthics> skos:definition
      "The guiding principles that define an organization’s culture."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TalentManagement>
    skos:definition "Attracting, developing and retaining top talent."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/JobProfile> skos:definition
      "A document that outlines the key responsibilities, skills, and qualifications required for a specific job."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OnboardingTraining>
    skos:definition "Integrating new hires into the organization and providing them with the necessary training and development."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RecruitmentSelection>
    skos:definition "Attracting and hiring qualified candidates for open positions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SkillsCompetencies>
    skos:definition "Identifying and developing the skills and competencies needed for organizational success."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WorkforcePlanning>
    skos:definition "Analyzing current and future workforce needs and developing strategies to meet those needs."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/HeadcountManagement>
    skos:definition "Planning and controlling the number of employees in an organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SuccessionPlanning>
    skos:definition "Identifying and developing employees for future leadership roles."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IntegratedServiceManagement>
    skos:definition "A holistic approach to managing all aspects of service delivery, from service design to customer support."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceChangeManagement>
    skos:definition "Managing changes to services to minimize disruptions and ensure a smooth transition."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceIncidentManagement>
    skos:definition "Responding to and resolving service interruptions or degradations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceProblem>
    skos:definition "The underlying cause of one or more service incidents."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceProblemReport>
    skos:definition "A formal record of a service problem, including details about the issue and any steps taken to resolve it."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceProblemResolution>
    skos:definition "The process of identifying and resolving the root cause of a service problem."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Intent> skos:definition
      "The underlying purpose or objective that drives an action or a business interaction."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Legal> skos:definition
      "The framework of rules and regulations that govern the conduct of businesses and individuals."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Compliance> skos:definition
      "Adhering to laws, regulations and industry standards."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ComplianceAudit>
    skos:definition "Assessing compliance with laws, regulations and policies."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ComplianceIncidentResponse>
    skos:definition "Responding to and investigating compliance violations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ComplianceMonitoring>
    skos:definition "Monitoring compliance with laws, regulations and policies."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ComplianceReporting>
    skos:definition "Reporting on compliance status to management and regulatory bodies."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ComplianceTraining>
    skos:definition "Educating employees on compliance obligations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PolicyDevelopment>
    skos:definition "Creating and implementing policies and procedures to ensure compliance."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Contracts> skos:definition
      "Legally binding agreements between two or more parties."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmploymentAgreement>
    skos:definition "A contract between an employer and an employee that outlines the terms and conditions of employment."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Leases> skos:definition
      "Contracts for the use of property or equipment for a specified period of time."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NonDisclosureAgreements>
    skos:definition "Agreements that protect confidential information."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SalesContract> skos:definition
      "An agreement for the sale of goods or services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CorporateLaw> skos:definition
      "The body of law that governs the formation, operation and dissolution of corporations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Incorporation> skos:definition
      "The legal process of forming a corporation."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MergersAcquisitions>
    skos:definition "The legal and financial processes involved in combining or acquiring other companies."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ShareholderRights>
    skos:definition "The legal rights of individuals or entities that own shares of stock in a corporation."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DisputeResolution>
    skos:definition "Resolving disagreements between parties."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Arbitration> skos:definition
      "A process in which a neutral third party hears evidence and makes a binding decision to resolve a dispute."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Litigation> skos:definition
      "The process of resolving a dispute through the court system."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Mediation> skos:definition
      "A process in which a neutral third party facilitates discussions between parties to help them reach a resolution."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Negotiation> skos:definition
      "Discussions between parties in an attempt to reach a mutually acceptable agreement."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmploymentLaw> skos:definition
      "The body of law that governs the employer-employee relationship."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Discrimination>
    skos:definition "Treating individuals differently based on protected characteristics, such as race, religion, or gender."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Firing> skos:definition
      "Terminating the employment relationship."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Harassment> skos:definition
      "Unwelcome conduct based on protected characteristics that creates a hostile work environment."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Hiring> skos:definition
      "The process of recruiting, interviewing and selecting employees."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Wages> skos:definition
      "Compensation paid to employees for their work."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WorkplaceSafety>
    skos:definition "Ensuring a safe and healthy work environment for employees."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IntellectualProperty>
    skos:definition "Intangible creations of the mind, such as inventions, literary and artistic works and symbols."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Copyright> skos:definition
      "Legal protection for original works of authorship."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Patents> skos:definition
      "Exclusive rights granted for inventions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TradeSecret> skos:definition
      "Confidential information that provides a business with a competitive advantage."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Trademarks> skos:definition
      "Distinctive signs that identify goods or services of a particular source."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Liability> skos:definition
      "Legal responsibility for harm caused to another person or entity."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EmployerLiability>
    skos:definition "Liability for the actions of employees."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EnvironmentalLiability>
    skos:definition "Liability for environmental contamination or damage."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductLiability>
    skos:definition "Liability for defects in products that cause injury or harm."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Location> skos:definition
      "A physical or geographical place associated with a party, such as an address or a set of coordinates."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Marketing> skos:definition
      "Strategies and activities aimed at promoting a company’s brand, products, or services to target audiences."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Advertising> skos:definition
      "Paid promotional messages delivered through various media channels, such as television, radio, print, online and social media."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Campaign> skos:definition
      "A coordinated series of marketing activities designed to achieve specific objectives, such as increasing brand awareness or driving sales."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MarketingCommunications>
    skos:definition "All forms of communication used to promote a company’s brand, products, or services, including advertising, public relations, content marketing and social media marketing."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BrandManagement>
    skos:definition "Developing and maintaining a strong brand identity and reputation."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Brand> skos:definition
      "A name, term, design, symbol, or other feature that identifies a company’s goods or services and distinguishes them from competitors."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BrandAwareness>
    skos:definition "The extent to which consumers are familiar with a brand and its products or services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BrandLeadership>
    skos:definition "Achieving a dominant position in the market based on brand strength and customer loyalty."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Competitor> skos:definition
      "A company that offers similar products or services and competes for the same target customers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CompetitiveIntelligence>
    skos:definition "The systematic and ethical process of gathering, analyzing, and distributing actionable information about the external business environment, with a primary focus on competitors, market trends, and customer behavior."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MarketDemographics>
    skos:definition "Statistical data about a population, such as age, gender, income, education and location."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MarketSegmentation>
    skos:definition "Dividing a market into distinct groups of customers with similar needs or characteristics."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/MarketStrategy>
    skos:definition "A comprehensive plan outlining how a company will reach its target market, position its products or services and achieve its marketing objectives."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Metric> skos:definition
      "Represent areas of business operation that are important in assessing business performance, customer satisfaction/loyalty and operational efficiency, typically following a preferred progression or a numerical directionality which indicates how the business is improving."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Network> skos:definition
      "A group of interconnected devices that can communicate with each other."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkBuild> skos:definition
      "The process of designing, deploying and configuring network infrastructure."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkCapacity>
    skos:definition "The maximum amount of data that a network can handle at a given time."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkConfiguration>
    skos:definition "The settings and parameters that control the operation of a network and its devices."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkOrchestration>
    skos:definition "Automating the configuration, management and coordination of network resources and services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkPerformance>
    skos:definition "The speed, reliability and efficiency of a network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CustomerNetworkPerformance>
    skos:definition "The quality of network service experienced by end users."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EthernetBackhaulPerformance>
    skos:definition "The performance of the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH), which affects the overall capacity and efficiency of the mobile network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FixedWirelessAccessPerformance>
    skos:definition "The performance of Fixed Wireless Access (FWA) connections, which affects the speed and reliability of internet access for customers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkEdgePerformance>
    skos:definition "The performance of edge computing resources, which affects the speed and latency of applications and services delivered to end users."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RadioAccessNetworkPerformance>
    skos:definition "The performance of the Radio Access Network (RAN), which affects the speed and reliability of mobile data services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkSpecification>
    skos:definition "A detailed description of the requirements and design of a network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkTopology>
    skos:definition "The physical or logical arrangement of devices and connections in a network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EthernetBackhaulTopology>
    skos:definition "The arrangement of network elements in the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH)"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkEdgeTopology>
    skos:definition "The arrangement of edge computing resources and connections."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RadioAccessNetworkTopology>
    skos:definition "The arrangement of cell towers, antennas and other components in the Radio Access Network (RAN)."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkUtilization>
    skos:definition "The amount of network capacity being used at a given time."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkInfrastructure>
    skos:definition "The physical and logical components that support the operation of a computer network, including hardware, software and protocols."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Transport> skos:definition
      "The movement of data across a network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EthernetBackhaul>
    skos:definition "Using wired Ethernet connections instead of wireless WiFi to transmit data between nodes in a mesh network or other distributed network setup. It provides a more stable and faster connection than Wi-Fi backhaul, ensuring a reliable data path between network devices."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IntelligentEdgeNetwork>
    skos:definition "A network architecture that distributes computing and networking resources closer to end users."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkEdge> skos:definition
      "The boundary between a company’s internal network and the internet or other external networks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RadioAccessNetwork>
    skos:definition "RAN, the part of a telecommunications system that connects mobile devices to the core network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Backbone> skos:definition
      "A high-speed, high-capacity network that forms the core of a larger network, connecting different parts of the network and providing a path for data to flow between them."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BigRockHomeInternet>
    skos:definition "It provides internet service via a 5G or 4G LTE connection, serving as an alternative to traditional cable or fiber internet."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PrivateMobileRadio>
    skos:definition "A land-mobile radio service able to use radio frequencies assigned to a specific organization or entity for private voice and data communication."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkOperationsCenterManagement>
    skos:definition "Overseeing and managing the operation and performance of a company’s network infrastructure."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkIncidentResponse>
    skos:definition "Responding to and resolving network incidents, such as outages, performance degradations and security breaches."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Alarm> skos:definition
      "A notification that indicates a potential problem or issue."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EthernetBackhaulFaultTelemetry>
    skos:definition "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in the Ethernet Backhaul (EBH)."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IntelligentEdgeNetworkFaultTelemetry>
    skos:definition "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in edge computing infrastructure."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RadioAccessNetworkFaultTelemetry>
    skos:definition "Alarms related to faults or performance issues in the Radio Access Network (RAN)."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Xdr> skos:definition
      "Extended Detection and Response, a security technology that provides comprehensive visibility and analysis of security threats across an organization’s entire IT infrastructure."@en;
    skos:altLabel "XDR"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IssueResolution>
    skos:definition "The process of identifying, diagnosing and resolving network infrastructure issues."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Patch> skos:definition
      "A software update that addresses vulnerabilities or bugs in a system."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Repair> skos:definition
      "Fixing a physical or logical defect in a device or system."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Technician> skos:definition
      "A skilled worker who installs, maintains and repairs technical equipment."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Test> skos:definition
      "A procedure intended to establish the quality, performance, or reliability of something, especially before it is taken into widespread use."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TruckRoll> skos:definition
      "Dispatching a technician to a customer’s location to resolve an issue."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WorkOrder> skos:definition
      "A formal request for work to be performed, such as a repair or installation."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkMonitoring>
    skos:definition "Continuously tracking the status and performance of network devices and services to identify and resolve issues proactively."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworkSecurity>
    skos:definition "Protecting network infrastructure and data from unauthorized access, use, disclosure, disruption, modification, or destruction."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OperationsManagement>
    skos:definition "The administration of business practices to create the highest level of efficiency possible within an organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AssuranceManagement>
    skos:definition "Providing confidence that an enterprise’s processes and systems are reliable and meet established standards."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AuditManagement>
    skos:definition "The process of conducting internal and external audits to provide independent assurance on an enterprise’s operations and financial reporting."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AuditEvidence> skos:definition
      "Information gathered by auditors to support their conclusions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AuditPlanning> skos:definition
      "Defining audit scope, objectives and procedures."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AuditReporting>
    skos:definition "Communicating audit findings and recommendations to management and the board of directors."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AuditRisk> skos:definition
      "The risk that an auditor may fail to detect material misstatements."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InternalControl>
    skos:definition "Processes and procedures implemented to ensure the accuracy and reliability of financial reporting and safeguard assets."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/QualityManagement>
    skos:definition "The processes and activities used to ensure that products or services meet customer expectations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ContinuousImprovement>
    skos:definition "Ongoing efforts to improve processes and products."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/QualityAssurance>
    skos:definition "Systematically reviewing and evaluating processes to ensure quality standards are met."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/QualityControl>
    skos:definition "Inspecting and testing products or services to identify and correct defects."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/QualityPlanning>
    skos:definition "Defining quality standards and developing plans to achieve them."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskManagement>
    skos:definition "The process of identifying, assessing and mitigating potential risks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskAssessment>
    skos:definition "Evaluating the likelihood and impact of potential risks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskIdentification>
    skos:definition "Determining potential threats to an enterprise."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskManagementLeadership>
    skos:definition "Promoting a culture of risk awareness and accountability."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskMonitoring>
    skos:definition "Tracking risks and the effectiveness of risk mitigation strategies."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/RiskResponse> skos:definition
      "Developing and implementing strategies to mitigate or manage risks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FulfillmentManagement>
    skos:definition "The processes involved in receiving, processing and fulfilling customer orders."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryManagement>
    skos:definition "The process of ordering, storing and tracking inventory levels."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryLocation>
    skos:definition "The physical location of inventory within a warehouse or storage facility."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryOptimization>
    skos:definition "Determining the optimal inventory levels to minimize costs and maximize efficiency."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryStatus>
    skos:definition "The current quantity of inventory on hand."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryTracking>
    skos:definition "Monitoring the movement of inventory throughout the supply chain."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InventoryValuation>
    skos:definition "Determining the monetary value of inventory."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OrderManagement>
    skos:definition "The process of receiving, tracking and fulfilling customer orders."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Delivery> skos:definition
      "The transportation of goods to customers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Installation> skos:definition
      "The process of setting up and configuring products for customers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Order> skos:definition
      "A request for goods or services placed by a customer."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OrderHistoryTracking>
    skos:definition "Maintaining records of past orders and providing customers with updates on the status of their orders."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OrderProcessing>
    skos:definition "The steps involved in preparing and shipping customer orders."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OrderQuote> skos:definition
      "An estimate of the cost of goods or services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ReturnsExchanges>
    skos:definition "Handling customer requests to return or exchange goods."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TransportationManagement>
    skos:definition "The selection, scheduling and monitoring of transportation providers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Fleet> skos:definition
      "A group of vehicles used for transportation purposes."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/WarehouseManagement>
    skos:definition "The management of warehouse operations, including receiving, storage and shipping."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/InformationProcessingManagement>
    skos:definition "The management of information technology systems and resources."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AutomatedResourceManagement>
    skos:definition "Using technology to automate the allocation and management of resources."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProcessAutomation>
    skos:definition "Using technology to automate business processes."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ResourceAllocation>
    skos:definition "Assigning resources to different tasks or projects."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BusinessIntelligence>
    skos:definition "Using data analysis to support business decision-making."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataAnalytics> skos:definition
      "Examining raw data to extract meaningful insights."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataManagement>
    skos:definition "The processes and policies for collecting, storing and using data."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataGovernance>
    skos:definition "Defining roles, responsibilities and processes for managing data assets."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataPrivacy> skos:definition
      "Protecting the personal information of individuals."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataQuality> skos:definition
      "Ensuring the accuracy, completeness and consistency of data."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataSecurity> skos:definition
      "Protecting data from unauthorized access, use, or disclosure."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EnterpriseResourcePlanningSystems>
    skos:definition "Integrated software systems that manage core business processes."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TransactionProcessingSystems>
    skos:definition "Systems that process and record routine business transactions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProjectProgramsManagement>
    skos:definition "The process of planning, executing and controlling projects and programs."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BusinessProcessReengineering>
    skos:definition "Radically redesigning business processes to achieve significant improvements."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProcessImprovement>
    skos:definition "Identifying and implementing ways to make business processes more efficient and effective."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProcessMapping>
    skos:definition "Visually representing business processes."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProjectExecution>
    skos:definition "Carrying out project tasks and activities."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProjectMonitoringControl>
    skos:definition "Tracking project progress and taking corrective action to ensure objectives are met."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProjectPlanning>
    skos:definition "Defining project scope, objectives and deliverables."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SecurityManagement>
    skos:definition "Protecting an enterprise’s information systems and data from unauthorized access, use, disclosure, disruption, modification, or destruction."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AttackManagement>
    skos:definition "Detecting, responding to and recovering from cyberattacks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IntrusionDetectionPrevention>
    skos:definition "Identifying and blocking malicious network activity."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SecurityInformationEventManagement>
    skos:definition "Collecting and analyzing security logs from multiple sources."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DisasterRecovery>
    skos:definition "Planning for and recovering from disasters that disrupt business operations."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/BusinessContinuityPlanning>
    skos:definition "Developing plans to ensure business operations can continue in the event of a disruption."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DataBackupRecovery>
    skos:definition "Regularly backing up data and having procedures in place to restore data in the event of loss or corruption."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/DisasterRecoveryTesting>
    skos:definition "Regularly testing disaster recovery plans to ensure they are effective."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ElementManagementSecurity>
    skos:definition "Securing individual components of an IT infrastructure."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CloudSecurity> skos:definition
      "Protecting data and applications stored in the cloud."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/EndpointSecurity>
    skos:definition "Securing devices that connect to a network."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/NetworksSecurity>
    skos:definition "Protecting networks from unauthorized access and attacks."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FirewallManagement>
    skos:definition "Configuring, monitoring and maintaining firewalls."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FirewallConfiguration>
    skos:definition "Defining firewall rules to control network traffic."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FirewallMaintenance>
    skos:definition "Updating firewall software and rules."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FirewallMonitoring>
    skos:definition "Tracking firewall activity and identifying potential threats."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FraudManagement>
    skos:definition "Detecting, preventing and investigating fraud."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FraudDetection>
    skos:definition "Identifying suspicious activities that may indicate fraud."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FraudInvestigation>
    skos:definition "Investigating suspected cases of fraud."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/FraudPrevention>
    skos:definition "Implementing measures to deter and prevent fraud."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/SpamManagement>
    skos:definition "Filtering and blocking unsolicited email messages."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ThreatManagement>
    skos:definition "Identifying, assessing and mitigating potential threats to an enterprise."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/UserAccountManagement>
    skos:definition "Managing user accounts and access privileges."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/IdentityManagement>
    skos:definition "Verifying and managing user identities."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/UserAuthentication>
    skos:definition "Verifying the identity of a user or device."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/UserAuthorization>
    skos:definition "Granting or denying access to resources based on user roles and permissions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/StrategicOperations>
    skos:definition "Aligning operations with overall business strategy."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/CostEffectivenessLeadership>
    skos:definition "Driving cost optimization initiatives across the organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/OperationsEfficiencyLeadership>
    skos:definition "Leading efforts to improve operational efficiency and productivity."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerAccount>
    skos:definition "Represents a business partner within a company’s systems, containing relevant information and interactions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AccountHierarchy>
    skos:definition "A structured representation of partner relationships, reflecting parent-child or subsidiary connections."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AccountSegmentation>
    skos:definition "Categorizing partner accounts based on specific criteria, such as revenue, industry, or partnership type."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ContactRole> skos:definition
      "Defines the specific function and responsibilities of an individual contact within a partner organization."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceAgreement>
    skos:definition "A formal document outlining the terms and conditions of service delivery between a company and its partner."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerContractManagement>
    skos:definition "Managing the lifecycle of contracts with business partners, including renewals and amendments."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerEcosystemManagement>
    skos:definition "The strategic oversight and coordination of a network of interconnected partners, fostering collaboration and value creation."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerIntegrationProcess>
    skos:definition "The steps involved in onboarding and integrating a new partner into a company’s systems and processes."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerPerformance>
    skos:definition "Evaluation of a partner’s effectiveness and contribution to shared goals."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerMarketShare>
    skos:definition "The percentage of a specific market controlled or influenced by a particular partner."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerRole> skos:definition
      "Defines the specific function and responsibilities of a business partner within the collaboration."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Dealer> skos:definition
      "An independent entity authorized to sell and distribute a company’s products to end customers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Partner> skos:definition
      "A general term encompassing various types of collaborative relationships, including resellers, distributors and technology providers."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PartnerSuccessOrganization>
    skos:definition "A dedicated strategic and operational business unit responsible for enabling, managing, and maximizing the mutual value of an enterprise’s indirect ecosystem—including resellers, system integrators (GSIs), managed service providers (MSPs), independent software vendors (ISVs), and referral agents—across their entire lifecycle to ensure sustained revenue growth, co-innovation, and joint customer satisfaction"@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Retailer> skos:definition
      "A business that sells goods directly to consumers through physical stores or online channels."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ServiceProvider>
    skos:definition "A company that delivers services, such as telecommunications, IT support, or consulting, to businesses or individuals."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Supplier> skos:definition
      "Similar to a vendor, but often implies a longer-term relationship and a focus on raw materials or components."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Vendor> skos:definition
      "An entity that supplies goods or services to another business, typically as part of a supply chain."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Party> skos:definition
      "An individual, organization, or group that can enter into relationships or transactions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Community> skos:definition
      "A grouping of parties that share a common interest, characteristic, or relationship."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ContactMedium> skos:definition
      "The method or channel through which communication or contact is made, such as email, phone, or social media."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Currency> skos:definition
      "A system of money in general use in a particular country, represented as a unit of account and a medium of exchange."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Demographic> skos:definition
      "Statistical data relating to a party, such as age, gender, income, or location, used for classification and analysis."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Identification>
    skos:definition "A unique characteristic or credential that serves to establish the identity of a party."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Organization> skos:definition
      "A type of party that is a legally recognized entity, such as a company, association, or government agency."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Permission> skos:definition
      "The authorization granted to a party to perform a specific action or access certain information."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Profile> skos:definition
      "A collection of data that provides a summary or overview of a particular party."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Role> skos:definition
      "The function or capacity in which a party acts in a particular context or relationship."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Skill> skos:definition
      "A specific ability or expertise possessed by a party."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Payment> skos:definition
      "Information related to the financial transactions and payment methods associated with a party."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Policy> skos:definition
      "A set of rules, guidelines, or principles that governs the actions and decisions of an organization or system."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PricingManagement>
    skos:definition "The processes and procedures of applying prices and discounts to the organization products & services."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PriceMarketResearch>
    skos:definition "Analyzing competitor pricing, understanding customer willingness to pay and identifying pricing trends."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PricePerception>
    skos:definition "How customers perceive the value of a product or service in relation to its price."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PricingStrategy>
    skos:definition "This includes concepts like cost-plus pricing, value-based pricing, competitive pricing, premium pricing, penetration pricing and dynamic pricing."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PricingTactics>
    skos:definition "Techniques like discounts, promotions, bundling and psychological pricing."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Bundle> skos:definition
      "A package of multiple products or services offered for sale together at a discounted price."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Discount> skos:definition
      "A reduction in the regular price of a product or service."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Offering> skos:definition
      "A specific product, service, or package offered for sale, often with associated pricing and terms."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Perks> skos:definition
      "Additional benefits or promotional offers associated with a particular service plan."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductPaymentPlan>
    skos:definition "Allowing customers to pay for a product over time through installments and includes includes the payment or payment plan (DPP) of the devices and also customer loan."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductRecycle>
    skos:definition "A program that allows customers to recycle old or unwanted products, often in exchange for a discount on a new purchase."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Promotions> skos:definition
      "A special offer available for a limited period, creating a sense of urgency to encourage purchases."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/TopUp> skos:definition
      "Adding additional credit or data to a prepaid mobile phone plan."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Trade> skos:definition
      "An exchange of goods or services, often involving a trade-in of an older product for a discount on a newer model."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Privacy> skos:definition
      "The right of a party to control the collection, use, and disclosure of their personal information."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductCapacity>
    skos:definition "The maximum output, volume, or number of users a product can handle or support effectively within a given timeframe and under specified conditions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductConfiguration>
    skos:definition "The process or result of customizing a product by selecting and arranging various options, components, or features to meet specific customer requirements or create distinct product variants."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductLifecycle>
    skos:definition "The stages a product goes through from its initial development to its eventual decline."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductDevelopment>
    skos:definition "The process of designing, creating and bringing a new product to market."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductResearchAnalysis>
    skos:definition "Gathering information about customer needs, market trends and competitive products to inform product development decisions."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductRoadmap>
    skos:definition "A high-level plan outlining the development timeline and key milestones for a product."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductVisionStrategy>
    skos:definition "Defining the overall direction and goals for a product or product line."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductPerformance>
    skos:definition "A measure of how well a product fulfills its intended purpose and meets user expectations, often evaluated through metrics related to its functionality, reliability, speed, efficiency, usability, and market success."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductPortfolio>
    skos:definition "The collection of all products or services offered by a company."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PortfolioStrategy>
    skos:definition "A plan outlining how a company will manage its product portfolio to achieve its business objectives, including decisions about product development, pricing and product lifecycle management."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ProductCatalog>
    skos:definition "A comprehensive list of a company’s products or services, often with descriptions, pricing and other relevant information."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/Accessories> skos:definition
      "Supplemental items that enhance the functionality or aesthetics of a core product, such as phone cases, screen protectors and headphones."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/AudioProducts> skos:definition
      "Products related to sound devices, such as headphones, earphones, speakers and microphones."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/ChargersCables>
    skos:definition "Power adapters and connecting cords used to charge electronic devices like smartphones, tablets and laptops."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/GamingProducts>
    skos:definition "Equipment and software designed for video games, including consoles, controllers and headsets."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/PhoneAttachments>
    skos:definition "External devices that enhance smartphone functionality, including lenses, grips and portable projectors."@en .
  
  <https://www.insperity.com/taxonomy/application-business-taxonomy/> skos:altLabel
      "Taxonomy | Application | Business Taxonomy"@en;
